    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(A)\\in[0.2,0.6]$, $P(B)\\in[0.2,0.6]$.\n\nEach event contains the intersection and lies within the union; their probabilities also satisfy $P(A)+P(B)=0.8$.",
      "worked": "Since $A\\cap B\\subseteq A\\subseteq A\\cup B$ and $A\\cap B\\subseteq B\\subseteq A\\cup B$,\n$$0.2\\le P(A)\\le 0.6,\\qquad 0.2\\le P(B)\\le 0.6.$$\nThe addition rule also gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)+P(B)&=P(A\\cup B)+P(A\\cap B)\\\\P(A)+P(B)&=0.6+0.2\\\\P(A)+P(B)&=0.8.\\end{align*}$$\nThe endpoint pairs $(P(A),P(B))=(0.2,0.6)$ and $(0.6,0.2)$ are attainable, with the smaller event contained in the larger.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
